1
00:00:15,432 --> 00:00:18,060
Sorry. Just a little longer.

2
00:00:20,820 --> 00:00:25,891
What does the after-party organizer
for a wedding actually do?

3
00:00:26,735 --> 00:00:30,030
Booking the venue,
planning the schedule, stuff like that.

4
00:00:30,030 --> 00:00:32,370
We can't make invitations
until we pick a place.

5
00:00:32,370 --> 00:00:35,090
And we need a video.

6
00:00:35,090 --> 00:00:38,260
It's not like you're that close with Moriya.

7
00:00:38,260 --> 00:00:41,100
You didn't have to take on
something so complicated.

8
00:00:41,100 --> 00:00:44,500
Well, I've organized after-parties
a few times before.

9
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:48,410
They said they'll let us
take care of everything.

10
00:00:49,020 --> 00:00:50,540
Us?

11
00:00:59,601 --> 00:01:02,419
Look at my phone anytime.

12
00:01:02,419 --> 00:01:03,380
What?

13
00:01:03,380 --> 00:01:07,550
The code is my employee number, 17135.

14
00:01:07,550 --> 00:01:09,400
What's this all of a sudden?

15
00:01:09,400 --> 00:01:12,840
I'm coordinating with the bride's organizer,

16
00:01:12,840 --> 00:01:16,170
so I might check my phone
or take calls while I'm with you.

17
00:01:16,170 --> 00:01:20,600
I might be alone with her
looking at places too, but don't worry.

18
00:01:20,600 --> 00:01:22,190
I'm not worried.

19
00:01:22,190 --> 00:01:24,340
Huh? Be worried.

20
00:01:26,837 --> 00:01:29,640
I'm kinda joking, but still...

21
00:01:29,640 --> 00:01:33,910
It'd make me feel better
if you look freely, okay?

22
00:01:35,920 --> 00:01:37,630
Really?

23
00:01:50,660 --> 00:01:52,350
Weird dog...

24
00:01:56,970 --> 00:01:59,280
You made this your pic?

25
00:01:59,280 --> 00:02:00,520
Yeah.

26
00:02:01,640 --> 00:02:04,490
Read the start of the chat.

27
00:02:04,490 --> 00:02:07,370
[Hi, it's Mitsuki!
Is that picture a sumo thing?]

28
00:02:07,370 --> 00:02:09,230
Sumo? Really?

29
00:02:09,230 --> 00:02:10,340
Right?

30
00:02:10,340 --> 00:02:12,830
I didn't know
sumo wrestlers used something similar.

31
00:02:12,830 --> 00:02:15,620
How old is she?
Is she just naturally like this?

32
00:02:15,620 --> 00:02:19,164
Same age as us, and normal.
A proper kind of person.

33
00:02:21,890 --> 00:02:23,210
Thanks.

34
00:02:23,870 --> 00:02:25,280
You're done?

35
00:02:25,280 --> 00:02:27,630
Because nothing looks suspicious.

36
00:02:27,630 --> 00:02:31,400
I mean, you could easily hide
whatever you don't want to show anyway.

37
00:02:31,400 --> 00:02:33,390
Then look at everything else too.

38
00:02:33,390 --> 00:02:35,290
Jeez, it's fine.

39
00:02:35,290 --> 00:02:37,570
Why do you want me to distrust you?

40
00:02:39,050 --> 00:02:40,750
It's not like that.

41
00:03:05,936 --> 00:03:10,176
<i>It started with an email.</i>

42
00:03:11,610 --> 00:03:15,890
[No Subject]
[Sorry for the late-night message.]

43
00:03:17,948 --> 00:03:19,608
<i>That's exactly why...</i>

44
00:03:46,100 --> 00:03:50,508
[Mitsuki: Does your company use
a slow juicer that you would recommend?]

45
00:04:58,859 --> 00:05:02,497
[Recommended Users]

46
00:05:06,640 --> 00:05:08,230
Weird dog...

47
00:05:16,810 --> 00:05:19,510
[Mi]

48
00:05:25,400 --> 00:05:27,710
Nakarai.

49
00:05:27,710 --> 00:05:33,120
IT just said it's about time
you change your computer password.

50
00:05:34,460 --> 00:05:37,770
They said you can't log in once it expires.

51
00:05:38,710 --> 00:05:41,660
Right. Thanks.

52
00:06:09,820 --> 00:06:13,264
[This password is already in use.]

53
00:06:25,240 --> 00:06:28,840
This Saturday,
I'm going a bit far out of town.

54
00:06:28,840 --> 00:06:30,820
- For the after-party?
- Yeah.

55
00:06:30,820 --> 00:06:33,080
The bride's grandpa lives in Gunma,

56
00:06:33,080 --> 00:06:35,520
so we're filming him as a surprise.

57
00:06:35,520 --> 00:06:39,200
He doesn't know
how to take videos on his phone.

58
00:06:39,860 --> 00:06:41,890
You're going with the girl?

59
00:06:42,710 --> 00:06:45,451
Yes. By rental car.

60
00:06:47,657 --> 00:06:49,730
That's a lot of work.

61
00:07:14,749 --> 00:07:19,053
[Wedding After-Party]

62
00:08:23,920 --> 00:08:26,130
[Mitsuki: How does this look?]

63
00:08:26,130 --> 00:08:28,880
[Wow, this looks amazing! Thank you!]

64
00:08:28,880 --> 00:08:31,250
[Glad I could help!]

65
00:08:43,180 --> 00:08:45,270
[Oh, gosh. He's totally my type.]

66
00:08:45,270 --> 00:08:48,060
[It wasn't a sumo tag.
I bet I seem so dumb.]

67
00:08:48,060 --> 00:08:51,480
[I wonder who he went
to the festival with. Was it a girl?]

68
00:08:51,480 --> 00:08:54,560
[It feels so nice being helpful.]

69
00:08:54,560 --> 00:08:58,478
[He said it looks great!
I'm gonna be happy for days.]

70
00:09:03,584 --> 00:09:06,209
Wait, where did I put my wallet?

71
00:09:06,209 --> 00:09:08,480
- Table for three.
- Right. This way, please.

72
00:09:09,750 --> 00:09:11,450
Oh, excuse me.

73
00:09:13,350 --> 00:09:14,640
Sorry,

74
00:09:14,640 --> 00:09:17,440
I need to go check out a venue tonight
for the after-party,

75
00:09:17,440 --> 00:09:19,360
so I can't come over tonight anymore.

76
00:09:19,360 --> 00:09:20,960
Sure, okay.

77
00:09:20,960 --> 00:09:22,760
I'll be in touch.

78
00:09:31,390 --> 00:09:33,830
Are you alone today?

79
00:09:33,830 --> 00:09:35,520
I am.

80
00:09:36,120 --> 00:09:37,130
The other day...

81
00:09:37,130 --> 00:09:39,690
Ayuko, come switch with me for a sec.

82
00:09:41,160 --> 00:09:42,610
Okay.

83
00:09:47,920 --> 00:09:51,590
[Mocchi showed me his ex's photo.
She's a beauty... I'm so depressed.]

84
00:09:51,590 --> 00:09:54,093
You dated for a long time, right?

85
00:09:54,093 --> 00:09:55,434
I guess so.

86
00:09:55,434 --> 00:09:58,134
Why did you break up with her?

87
00:09:59,224 --> 00:10:01,894
Well, a lot happened.

88
00:10:03,390 --> 00:10:05,000
A lot...

89
00:10:08,960 --> 00:10:12,990
Sorry, I overstepped just now.

90
00:10:12,990 --> 00:10:14,890
No, it's totally fine.

91
00:10:29,600 --> 00:10:31,450
<i>I'll be back by night.</i>

92
00:10:33,280 --> 00:10:34,640
Okay.

93
00:10:34,640 --> 00:10:37,020
Drive safe.

94
00:10:37,020 --> 00:10:39,350
<i>Yes. I'll drive carefully.</i>

95
00:10:39,350 --> 00:10:41,540
<i>- See you.</i>
- Okay.

96
00:10:49,140 --> 00:10:52,240
<i>I wanted to make lunch for tomorrow's trip,</i>

97
00:10:52,240 --> 00:10:56,860
<i>but he said he'd find
a tasty restaurant for us nearby.</i>

98
00:10:56,860 --> 00:11:00,100
<i>That's kind of him, but ruthless too.</i>

99
00:11:03,540 --> 00:11:06,271
<i>But I'm looking forward to tomorrow.</i>

100
00:11:06,271 --> 00:11:09,167
<i>What is wrong with me?</i>

101
00:11:10,030 --> 00:11:14,020
<i>Will he notice I got new nails?</i>

102
00:11:14,800 --> 00:11:19,110
<i>I wonder what kind of fashion he likes.</i>

103
00:11:22,630 --> 00:11:24,300
Welcome.

104
00:11:40,800 --> 00:11:45,920
<i>And he's so cool, with long fingers.</i>

105
00:11:45,920 --> 00:11:47,440
<i>His fingers too.</i>

106
00:11:50,390 --> 00:11:53,197
<i>A girl on this earth gets to</i>

107
00:11:53,197 --> 00:11:56,700
<i>intertwine her fingers
with those fingers of his.</i>

108
00:11:56,700 --> 00:11:59,290
This color seems like you, Nakarai.

109
00:12:06,079 --> 00:12:10,729
<i>I know there's nothing between us.
But still...</i>

110
00:12:18,572 --> 00:12:20,036
That's tasty.

111
00:12:24,720 --> 00:12:29,450
<i>I want to stare
at the side of his handsome face forever.</i>

112
00:12:38,091 --> 00:12:39,959
Sorry.

113
00:12:39,959 --> 00:12:41,529
Come on.

114
00:12:54,690 --> 00:12:55,750
Hello?

115
00:12:55,750 --> 00:12:58,310
<i>Nakarai! Help me!</i>

116
00:12:58,310 --> 00:12:59,500
Huh?

117
00:13:09,170 --> 00:13:11,165
Sorry, Nakarai.

118
00:13:11,165 --> 00:13:13,130
No one else would pick up.

119
00:13:13,130 --> 00:13:15,850
It's okay. I've done it too.

120
00:13:20,020 --> 00:13:22,830
Working on a day off is rough.

121
00:13:29,700 --> 00:13:31,720
I'm not working.

122
00:13:32,920 --> 00:13:35,340
I didn't want to be at home.

123
00:13:36,030 --> 00:13:37,590
Is something wrong?

124
00:13:38,400 --> 00:13:40,520
Will you hear me out?

125
00:13:40,520 --> 00:13:41,810
Sure.

126
00:13:43,220 --> 00:13:47,740
There's this idol I Stan,

127
00:13:48,410 --> 00:13:50,940
and a dating scandal came out yesterday.

128
00:13:52,380 --> 00:13:55,234
So when I was alone at home
agonizing over it,

129
00:13:55,234 --> 00:13:57,060
I couldn't take it.

130
00:13:57,740 --> 00:14:00,630
So I ran away to the office.

131
00:14:01,310 --> 00:14:03,250
I see.

132
00:14:04,927 --> 00:14:08,140
I might not be able
to support him anymore...

133
00:14:08,830 --> 00:14:12,250
But I guess that can't be helped.

134
00:14:14,870 --> 00:14:16,240
All right.

135
00:14:16,240 --> 00:14:18,930
I'm gonna do Pilates five days a week.

136
00:14:18,930 --> 00:14:19,860
Huh?

137
00:14:19,860 --> 00:14:24,240
I wanna channel these feelings
into something positive, you know?

138
00:14:24,240 --> 00:14:28,400
It's not like I can tell him
how I feel in person.

139
00:14:30,162 --> 00:14:34,492
And I don't want to regret falling for him.

140
00:14:37,430 --> 00:14:38,440
Oh, right.

141
00:14:38,440 --> 00:14:41,990
I'll give you a proper thank-you later,
but here.

142
00:14:41,990 --> 00:14:44,400
- What's this?
- It was a gift.

143
00:14:44,400 --> 00:14:46,830
Apparently it tastes good soaked in whiskey.

144
00:14:57,530 --> 00:14:59,660
I'm home.

145
00:14:59,660 --> 00:15:01,390
Sorry I'm late.

146
00:15:01,390 --> 00:15:03,470
Traffic was bad.

147
00:15:05,754 --> 00:15:07,294
Nakarai?

148
00:15:09,050 --> 00:15:12,361
Sorry, were you waiting up for me?

149
00:15:14,350 --> 00:15:16,740
Huh? Are you drunk?

150
00:15:18,168 --> 00:15:20,210
What's that?

151
00:15:20,210 --> 00:15:22,170
Gummies.

152
00:15:22,170 --> 00:15:24,440
Those aren't just gummies.

153
00:15:25,920 --> 00:15:28,540
They reek of alcohol.

154
00:15:30,010 --> 00:15:31,950
While I was waiting at home,

155
00:15:31,950 --> 00:15:36,010
I wanted something to snack on,
and I couldn't stop.

156
00:15:37,500 --> 00:15:39,680
You wanted something to snack on?

157
00:15:42,210 --> 00:15:46,250
Hagiwara, don't you have something to say?

158
00:15:46,250 --> 00:15:47,250
Huh?

159
00:15:47,250 --> 00:15:49,790
Anything you wanna tell me?

160
00:15:49,790 --> 00:15:51,530
Huh?

161
00:15:51,530 --> 00:15:53,170
No, not really...

162
00:15:53,170 --> 00:15:54,540
Liar.

163
00:15:54,540 --> 00:15:56,350
What?

164
00:15:56,350 --> 00:15:58,110
There isn't. Really.

165
00:15:58,110 --> 00:16:00,270
Think harder.

166
00:16:00,270 --> 00:16:01,790
Huh?

167
00:16:04,060 --> 00:16:05,790
There's nothing to say.

168
00:16:05,790 --> 00:16:08,890
No guilty secrets.
Cheating is out of the question.

169
00:16:08,890 --> 00:16:11,080
And no group dates either.

170
00:16:17,270 --> 00:16:19,800
I have something to say to you.

171
00:16:19,800 --> 00:16:22,030
Huh? You do?

172
00:16:22,030 --> 00:16:24,890
What? You're scaring me.

173
00:16:27,360 --> 00:16:31,590
I looked at your phone, Hagiwara.

174
00:16:32,220 --> 00:16:34,970
The one where you're messaging that girl.

175
00:16:35,660 --> 00:16:37,020
Sorry.

176
00:16:38,410 --> 00:16:40,640
What? That's all?

177
00:16:40,640 --> 00:16:43,530
I said you could look. It's totally fine.

178
00:16:43,530 --> 00:16:45,270
That's not all.

179
00:16:46,060 --> 00:16:50,410
I found her social media account
and looked at it.

180
00:16:51,470 --> 00:16:53,610
Seriously?

181
00:16:53,610 --> 00:16:56,960
Well, I haven't done anything
I'd need to keep secret.

182
00:16:59,260 --> 00:17:01,800
I was like, "Dammit".

183
00:17:01,800 --> 00:17:03,090
Huh?

184
00:17:04,120 --> 00:17:06,870
The way that girl sees you, Hagiwara,

185
00:17:06,870 --> 00:17:09,550
is as a capable, organized guy.

186
00:17:09,550 --> 00:17:12,550
Kind and polite,

187
00:17:13,210 --> 00:17:15,210
with beautiful fingers.

188
00:17:15,210 --> 00:17:17,020
Thank you?

189
00:17:17,650 --> 00:17:22,750
But even after falling for you,
you didn't give her any openings.

190
00:17:23,720 --> 00:17:27,100
Yet every little thing you did
would excite her.

191
00:17:29,740 --> 00:17:33,950
We didn't have that kind of thing.

192
00:17:35,240 --> 00:17:41,310
Even before we thought about love,
we got close and had sex.

193
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:45,510
True.

194
00:17:48,610 --> 00:17:54,630
The things we skipped over
were there on her social media.

195
00:18:04,890 --> 00:18:06,690
So, I...

196
00:18:08,960 --> 00:18:13,890
fell for you again through her eyes.

197
00:18:17,810 --> 00:18:21,170
So, after I fell in love,
I fell in love again.

198
00:18:24,897 --> 00:18:26,758
Darn it.

199
00:18:28,560 --> 00:18:32,090
Hey, stop that.

200
00:18:36,440 --> 00:18:38,400
Anything else to say?

201
00:18:40,400 --> 00:18:43,400
I was jealous that you went out together too.

202
00:18:46,420 --> 00:18:48,910
Let's go out when things settle down.

203
00:19:08,790 --> 00:19:09,900
Let's eat gummies.

204
00:19:09,900 --> 00:19:10,990
You look sleepy.

205
00:19:10,990 --> 00:19:12,640
- Gummies!
- Huh?

206
00:19:21,940 --> 00:19:24,700
[Oh, gosh. Just seeing her in her dress
made me cry.]

207
00:19:24,700 --> 00:19:28,068
[He left in a hurry.
I can tell he has someone he likes.]

208
00:19:35,030 --> 00:19:36,620
Nakarai!

209
00:19:45,500 --> 00:19:47,370
Why are you laughing?

210
00:19:47,370 --> 00:19:48,830
It's nothing.

211
00:19:49,880 --> 00:19:51,821
You're finally back.

212
00:20:04,010 --> 00:20:07,290
By the way, what happened the other night?

213
00:20:07,290 --> 00:20:10,330
The "anything wanna tell me?" thing.

214
00:20:10,330 --> 00:20:11,877
What's that?

215
00:20:11,877 --> 00:20:13,770
Did I say that?

216
00:20:13,770 --> 00:20:16,210
Huh? You don't remember?

217
00:20:16,210 --> 00:20:18,910
You pressed me really hard.

218
00:20:18,910 --> 00:20:22,750
You kept asking,
"Don't you have something to say to me?"

219
00:20:23,550 --> 00:20:25,190
Don't brush this off!

220
00:20:25,190 --> 00:20:27,590
So, what was that about?

221
00:20:27,590 --> 00:20:29,210
I had no idea what you meant.

222
00:20:29,210 --> 00:20:31,760
I thought so much, I couldn't sleep.

223
00:20:33,540 --> 00:20:35,400
Oh, I remember.

224
00:20:35,400 --> 00:20:36,580
What?

225
00:20:36,580 --> 00:20:38,570
The password.

226
00:20:38,570 --> 00:20:39,720
Huh?

227
00:20:39,720 --> 00:20:41,700
The company login password.

228
00:20:41,700 --> 00:20:44,270
You used my name, didn't you?

229
00:20:46,538 --> 00:20:49,410
Oh, that?

230
00:20:49,410 --> 00:20:51,170
When I tried to use it,

231
00:20:51,170 --> 00:20:54,370
it said, "This password is already in use".

232
00:20:55,710 --> 00:20:57,640
It might not be me though.

233
00:20:57,640 --> 00:21:00,970
For example,
maybe someone has a crush on you.

234
00:21:00,970 --> 00:21:02,980
But it was you, right?

235
00:21:04,280 --> 00:21:05,770
You caught me.

236
00:21:06,930 --> 00:21:10,210
Is it fun using my name and birthday?

237
00:21:10,210 --> 00:21:11,460
Password thief.

238
00:21:11,460 --> 00:21:15,310
Because every time I enter my password,
I think of you, Nakarai.

239
00:21:15,310 --> 00:21:16,930
Nice, right?

240
00:21:21,360 --> 00:21:23,200
If you do that,

241
00:21:23,200 --> 00:21:27,220
I'll run out of words I can use
for my passwords.

242
00:21:27,220 --> 00:21:30,840
Let's not use each other's info
in our passwords.

243
00:21:30,840 --> 00:21:32,400
What?

244
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:36,090
A mutual non-aggression pact.

245
00:21:36,090 --> 00:21:37,620
Okay.

246
00:21:40,820 --> 00:21:42,301
A wedding favor?

247
00:21:42,301 --> 00:21:45,806
Yeah. I got one... Huh? Wait, what?

248
00:21:48,058 --> 00:21:50,468
Oh, I see.

249
00:21:52,020 --> 00:21:54,020
It's raining again, huh?

250
00:21:54,020 --> 00:21:55,680
It's not me.

251
00:21:56,984 --> 00:21:58,954
This rain's pretty heavy.

252
00:22:00,570 --> 00:22:01,810
I'm home.

253
00:22:01,810 --> 00:22:03,230
I'm home.

254
00:22:04,120 --> 00:22:05,780
What was the wedding favor?

255
00:22:05,780 --> 00:22:07,900
Just wait a second.

256
00:22:24,250 --> 00:22:27,988
[Thank you]
[Vostok]

257
00:22:31,101 --> 00:22:34,325
[Vostok Designer]
[Kazuaki Fujisawa]

258
00:22:35,910 --> 00:22:37,790
What is it?

259
00:22:37,790 --> 00:22:39,140
Glasses.

260
00:22:40,850 --> 00:22:41,945
Can I see?

261
00:22:41,945 --> 00:22:43,195
Go ahead.

262
00:22:53,940 --> 00:22:57,800
They're tilting,
but like they're leaning on each other.

263
00:22:58,560 --> 00:22:59,910
Yeah.

264
00:23:08,549 --> 00:23:10,239
They're well-made.

265
00:23:15,200 --> 00:23:17,070
Shall we toast?

266
00:23:17,070 --> 00:23:18,750
To what?

267
00:23:18,750 --> 00:23:21,720
To an ordinary day, I guess.

268
00:23:22,470 --> 00:23:24,060
Oh, jeez.

269
00:23:33,410 --> 00:23:36,310
A toast to an ordinary day. Cheers.

270
00:23:36,310 --> 00:23:37,780
Cheers.

271
00:23:45,610 --> 00:23:48,060
- A girl from a normal family, huh?
- In this day and age?

272
00:23:48,060 --> 00:23:49,970
Be nice to your parents when they're alive.

273
00:23:49,970 --> 00:23:52,598
What could I possibly do or say
in response to that?

274
00:23:52,598 --> 00:23:55,700
That just means everyone wants
what's best for other people.

275
00:23:55,700 --> 00:23:57,600
Ask more. "Is it mine?"

276
00:23:57,600 --> 00:23:59,010
Is it mine?
